From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:42:06 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: spoof home Wi-Fi NetworkInformation natively

Expose a native EventTarget-derived NetworkInformation with Chrome desktop
members: onchange, effectiveType, rtt, downlink and saveData. Cache connection
privately on each Navigator/WorkerNavigator wrapper for SameObject identity
without crossing isolated-world prototypes. Register Window and all worker
exposures; leave NetInfoDownlinkMax-gated members absent.

Model the Neo browsing from a US household over Wi-Fi on a representative
300/20 Mbps cable plan. Report fixed 4g, 10 Mbps downlink, 50 ms HTTP RTT and
saveData=false. The reported throughput is Chrome's capped estimate, not
ISP-plan bandwidth; no host measurement, shaping, synthetic periodic events
or HTTP hint support is added. See parent AGENTS.md for the network persona.

Implement onchange with a stable native listener, preserving ordering across
replacement, removal and re-addition. Reuse EventManagerBase for listeners,
abort/once semantics and dispatch. Allocate per execution scope and dispatch
through the current valid execution context; retain no raw context pointer.
This keeps retained iframe connections safe after child navigation.

References:
- Chromium 155.0.8059.40 modules/netinfo/network_information.idl and
  navigator_network_information.idl: exposed members and SameObject binding
- Chromium 155.0.8059.40 platform/network/network_state_notifier.cc:
  10 Mbps cap and 50 kbps / 50 ms estimate quantization
- https://www.optimum.com/articles/internet/average-home-internet-speed
  for context on a representative household plan, not measured averages

Validation: dev build; all 1658 existing upstream tests; 54/54 temporary CDP
checks including isolated-world surface/events, dedicated/shared/service
worker checks and an iframe connection retained across child navigation.
No new unit tests or benchmark changes.
